{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-harmonic-form","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-harmonic-form","kind":"definition","title":"Particle ($q$-harmonic form)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv"],"tags":["particle","harmonic"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QHarmonicForm","text":"q-harmonic-form.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-form.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-harmonic-form\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed exterior derivative <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q</code>. The <em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian</em> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^k(A)</code> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q = d_q\\delta_q + \\delta_qd_q</code>. A <strong>particle</strong> is an element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha \\in \\Omega^k(A)</code> that is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-harmonic: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q \\alpha = 0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-form.md","heading":"Definition","number":"3.15.4"}
